1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,133
They had crossed a border for a timetable; now the deadline was inside one body.

2
00:00:05,133 --> 00:00:14,623
The sixth arc opened with a crisis that nobody had anticipated: Daniel collapsed on the last step of the sports center ladder.

3
00:00:14,623 --> 00:00:29,882
An athlete of national standard, a scout for a professional club, and a sportswoman who trained with him three times a week all said the same thing: he had been eating the food of one nap and sleeping four hours.

4
00:00:29,882 --> 00:00:33,687
“It was not a weapon,” the doctor said.

5
00:00:33,687 --> 00:00:37,002
“It was a situation.”

6
00:00:37,002 --> 00:00:41,366
I hope this becomes a lesson, not a story.

7
00:00:41,366 --> 00:00:54,256
The concept of improvement had been pressed on him by everyone: a bunch of small gains, a particle at a time, a dosage of training that would make him curable and quick.

8
00:00:54,256 --> 00:00:59,535
“You cannot persuade a body with emphasis,” the doctor said.

9
00:00:59,535 --> 00:01:11,164
“You can only assist it.” A cosmic disturbance, a whale, a famine, and the strike of the grocers were the metaphors the team invented to explain the delay.

10
00:01:11,164 --> 00:01:15,209
Make it simple, they said.

11
00:01:15,209 --> 00:01:22,964
The reunion of the old rowing crew was still a week away, and the refrigerator in the common room was empty.

12
00:01:22,964 --> 00:01:31,959
Follow the training plan, the coach said; take the lift, send the form, and bring the ladder back.

13
00:01:31,959 --> 00:01:34,784
Who would make the first step?

14
00:01:34,784 --> 00:01:46,303
Our answer came from the church clinic, an hour north of the campus, where an inhabitant of the old town had starved himself into the same ward.

15
00:01:46,303 --> 00:01:58,637
The disturbance was measurable: a diameter of two centimetres in the ankle, a pulse of a hundred and ten, and a weight that had dropped farther than any of them had guessed.

16
00:01:58,637 --> 00:02:02,862
“You cannot escape a body,” the doctor said.

17
00:02:02,862 --> 00:02:15,996
“You can only involve it in the plan.” A disabled swimmer and a surfer with a bad chin had both been through the same ward, and both had come back through the same door.

18
00:02:15,996 --> 00:02:25,950
The last item on the sheet was the hardest: the sportsman who could not rest, the god of the timetable, the over-full week.

19
00:02:25,950 --> 00:02:30,835
“Training is not a punishment,” Daniel said at last.

20
00:02:30,835 --> 00:02:39,845
“Kill that idea and I will follow the plan.” An athlete had made the promise; a person would have to keep it.

21
00:02:39,845 --> 00:02:47,279
The question was not whether anyone could work harder; it was whether the change could take place at all.

22
00:02:47,279 --> 00:02:54,711
Nothing could induce him to sleep, and the week was over before the plan existed.
